=== Module 19 - Recursive-Descent Parsing ===

grammar (no left recursion; Module 23 derives this from  E -> E + T):
  E  -> T E'
  E' -> + T E'  |  epsilon
  T  -> F T'
  T' -> * F T'  |  epsilon
  F  -> ( E )   |  num  |  id
  one method per nonterminal; the productions they fire ARE a leftmost derivation

--- 1 + 2 * 3 ---
  tokens:  num(1) + num(2) * num(3) EOF
  productions fired, in order (top of the list = first call):
      E -> T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> num
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> + T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> num
      T' -> * F T'
      F -> num
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> epsilon
  same list, replayed as a leftmost derivation:
      E
      =>  T E'                     (E -> T E')
      =>  F T' E'                  (T -> F T')
      =>  num T' E'                (F -> num)
      =>  num E'                   (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  num + T E'               (E' -> + T E')
      =>  num + F T' E'            (T -> F T')
      =>  num + num T' E'          (F -> num)
      =>  num + num * F T' E'      (T' -> * F T')
      =>  num + num * num T' E'    (F -> num)
      =>  num + num * num E'       (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  num + num * num          (E' -> epsilon)
  derived sentence: num + num * num
  token kinds     : num + num * num
  match? true
  concrete syntax tree:
    E
    +- T
    |  +- F
    |  |  +- num (1)
    |  +- T'
    |     +- epsilon
    +- E'
       +- +
       +- T
       |  +- F
       |  |  +- num (2)
       |  +- T'
       |     +- *
       |     +- F
       |     |  +- num (3)
       |     +- T'
       |        +- epsilon
       +- E'
          +- epsilon
  yield: num + num * num

--- (1 + 2) * 3 ---
  tokens:  ( num(1) + num(2) ) * num(3) EOF
  productions fired, in order (top of the list = first call):
      E -> T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> ( E )
      E -> T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> num
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> + T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> num
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> epsilon
      T' -> * F T'
      F -> num
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> epsilon
  same list, replayed as a leftmost derivation:
      E
      =>  T E'                     (E -> T E')
      =>  F T' E'                  (T -> F T')
      =>  ( E ) T' E'              (F -> ( E ))
      =>  ( T E' ) T' E'           (E -> T E')
      =>  ( F T' E' ) T' E'        (T -> F T')
      =>  ( num T' E' ) T' E'      (F -> num)
      =>  ( num E' ) T' E'         (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  ( num + T E' ) T' E'     (E' -> + T E')
      =>  ( num + F T' E' ) T' E'  (T -> F T')
      =>  ( num + num T' E' ) T' E' (F -> num)
      =>  ( num + num E' ) T' E'   (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  ( num + num ) T' E'      (E' -> epsilon)
      =>  ( num + num ) * F T' E'  (T' -> * F T')
      =>  ( num + num ) * num T' E' (F -> num)
      =>  ( num + num ) * num E'   (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  ( num + num ) * num      (E' -> epsilon)
  derived sentence: ( num + num ) * num
  token kinds     : ( num + num ) * num
  match? true
  concrete syntax tree:
    E
    +- T
    |  +- F
    |  |  +- (
    |  |  +- E
    |  |  |  +- T
    |  |  |  |  +- F
    |  |  |  |  |  +- num (1)
    |  |  |  |  +- T'
    |  |  |  |     +- epsilon
    |  |  |  +- E'
    |  |  |     +- +
    |  |  |     +- T
    |  |  |     |  +- F
    |  |  |     |  |  +- num (2)
    |  |  |     |  +- T'
    |  |  |     |     +- epsilon
    |  |  |     +- E'
    |  |  |        +- epsilon
    |  |  +- )
    |  +- T'
    |     +- *
    |     +- F
    |     |  +- num (3)
    |     +- T'
    |        +- epsilon
    +- E'
       +- epsilon
  yield: ( num + num ) * num

--- a ---
  tokens:  id(a) EOF
  productions fired, in order (top of the list = first call):
      E -> T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> id
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> epsilon
  same list, replayed as a leftmost derivation:
      E
      =>  T E'                     (E -> T E')
      =>  F T' E'                  (T -> F T')
      =>  id T' E'                 (F -> id)
      =>  id E'                    (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  id                       (E' -> epsilon)
  derived sentence: id
  token kinds     : id
  match? true
  concrete syntax tree:
    E
    +- T
    |  +- F
    |  |  +- id (a)
    |  +- T'
    |     +- epsilon
    +- E'
       +- epsilon
  yield: id

--- a + b + c ---
  tokens:  id(a) + id(b) + id(c) EOF
  productions fired, in order (top of the list = first call):
      E -> T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> id
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> + T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> id
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> + T E'
      T -> F T'
      F -> id
      T' -> epsilon
      E' -> epsilon
  same list, replayed as a leftmost derivation:
      E
      =>  T E'                     (E -> T E')
      =>  F T' E'                  (T -> F T')
      =>  id T' E'                 (F -> id)
      =>  id E'                    (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  id + T E'                (E' -> + T E')
      =>  id + F T' E'             (T -> F T')
      =>  id + id T' E'            (F -> id)
      =>  id + id E'               (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  id + id + T E'           (E' -> + T E')
      =>  id + id + F T' E'        (T -> F T')
      =>  id + id + id T' E'       (F -> id)
      =>  id + id + id E'          (T' -> epsilon)
      =>  id + id + id             (E' -> epsilon)
  derived sentence: id + id + id
  token kinds     : id + id + id
  match? true
  concrete syntax tree:
    E
    +- T
    |  +- F
    |  |  +- id (a)
    |  +- T'
    |     +- epsilon
    +- E'
       +- +
       +- T
       |  +- F
       |  |  +- id (b)
       |  +- T'
       |     +- epsilon
       +- E'
          +- +
          +- T
          |  +- F
          |  |  +- id (c)
          |  +- T'
          |     +- epsilon
          +- E'
             +- epsilon
  yield: id + id + id

--- 1 + ---
  tokens:  num(1) + EOF
  SYNTAX ERROR at position 3: expected '(', num, or id to start a factor but saw end of input

--- (1 + 2 ---
  tokens:  ( num(1) + num(2) EOF
  SYNTAX ERROR at position 6: expected ) but saw end of input

--- 1 2 ---
  tokens:  num(1) num(2) EOF
  SYNTAX ERROR at position 2: expected EOF but saw '2'

why not parse the Module 6 grammar  E -> E + T  directly?
  parseE() would call parseE() as its first action, cursor unmoved:
  infinite recursion, stack overflow, zero tokens consumed. Recursive
  descent REQUIRES a non-left-recursive grammar (Module 23). The right-
  recursive E' here makes  a + b + c  lean RIGHT in the tree; left
  associativity is put back when lowering to an AST (Module 39), or by
  writing E' as a loop:
      Node e = parseT();
      while (at("+")) { expect("+"); e = plus(e, parseT()); }   // left-leaning
